        "id": 183102,
        "name": "UXM266",
        "username": "UXM266",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/uxm266/{size}/1966_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-11-01T20:19:53.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Also, I've been reading Saga since it was recomended here UXM. I gotta be honest. I love it so far. I'm having a hard time putting it down.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Around Volumr 5 it starts really not heading anywhere, and tends to use too many \"NEXT PAGE IS A SHOCKER\" kind of moments. but it's still solid. Beautifully drawn (I got a sketch from Fiona Staples!) and well written. Also, the \"blue\" language is esperanto!</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Glad you like it!</p>",
